      "problem": "A data set has a mean $\\overset{¯}{x}=14.5$ and an unknown standard deviation. An observation of the data set has the value $x=20$ and $z$-score $z=2.2.$ Find the standard deviation of the data set.",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=20,$ $\\overset{¯}{x}=14.5,$ and $z=2.2$ into the formula and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 20 & =14.5+2.2\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 5.5 & =2.2\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
